  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="f335-64a6-acd9-3974" name="Republican Indian (AoA2) - List Notes" publicationId="fcb9-17be-94c2-bcfc" hidden="false">
      <description>ARMIES OF ANTIQUITY v2 #10 (unofficial, Martin Gibbins). This list covers the states of North Western India not ruled by Kings or Princes, from the adoption of the heavy chariot until absorbed into the Mauryan Empire. Many of these states put up a fierce resistance to Alexander the Great. 

ARMY COMPOSITION:
[Republican Indian]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Chariotry and Cavalry: up to 33%
  Infantry: at least 25%
  Wagons: up to 20%
  Characters: up to 25% Chariotry and Cavalry: up to 33% Infantry: At least 25% Wagons: up to 20%</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
